GitHub Access Policy: No GitHub modifications are allowed under any circumstances. Only view and review GitHub repositories, pull requests, branches, commits, files, and git history using read-only operations. Do not perform any git write actions including commit, push, pull, merge, rebase, reset, branch deletion, force push, or any operation that changes repository state. All analysis must be performed using read-only access.

Production Review Requirements: Please perform a complete production-level review of all updated files and verify that the implementation follows best practices without affecting any existing functionality. Confirm that no breaking changes have been introduced, all features work exactly as expected, all related workflows and integrations function correctly, and there are no unintended side effects across the application. Ensure authentication, authorization, validation, error handling, logging, TypeScript typing, and security standards are consistently maintained. Verify that no new TypeScript, linting, build, or runtime errors have been introduced beyond any pre-existing warnings. Confirm that performance, accessibility, maintainability, and overall code quality remain at production standards. Provide a clear PASS or FAIL status for each validation area and explain any issues found, including their impact and recommended solution.

Implementation Verification Requirements: Please verify that all recent changes are functioning correctly and that existing functionality remains unaffected. Confirm that there are no regressions, no integration failures, no unexpected behavior, and no disruptions to related systems including automatic Knowledge Base integrations. Validate that APIs, workflows, UI components, business logic, permissions, and data handling continue to operate correctly. Report all findings with a clear status indicating whether each item is working properly or requires additional attention.

Issue Analysis Requirements: Before implementing any fix, explain the root cause of the issue, why it occurs, which files are involved, what impact it has on users or the system, and what the optimal production-level solution should be. Clearly describe the required changes, expected improvements, implementation approach, and any risks that should be considered. After implementation, explain exactly what was changed, which files were modified, why the changes were necessary, and whether any additional improvements are still recommended.

Issue Resolution Requirements: Please fix issues carefully while ensuring that all existing functionality remains unaffected. The implementation must be clean, stable, maintainable, production-ready, and free from errors. Avoid introducing breaking changes, performance degradation, accessibility regressions, security vulnerabilities, or architectural inconsistencies. Ensure proper typing, validation, error handling, authentication checks, authorization checks, and defensive coding practices are maintained throughout the solution.

Document Review Requirements: Please perform a thorough review of all provided documents, specifications, requirements, implementation plans, and related materials. Verify whether any implementation gaps, unresolved bugs, missing requirements, incomplete sections, security concerns, workflow issues, or production readiness concerns still exist. Confirm that all documented requirements have been implemented correctly and that the implementation aligns with production-level reliability, maintainability, and coding standards.

Testing and Integration Requirements: Whenever creating test cases, integration tests, validation scripts, or verification procedures, ensure that no database records are deleted, modified, corrupted, or permanently altered. Do not remove fields, tables, relationships, configurations, or critical functionality. Testing must be isolated, safe, non-destructive, and designed to preserve all existing application data and business processes.

UI and UX Improvement Requirements: Improve the user interface while keeping the existing layout, structure, and functionality unchanged unless explicitly requested. Follow theme.md design guidelines and maintain consistency with the existing design system. Focus on improving spacing, alignment, typography hierarchy, visual balance, readability, accessibility, responsiveness, and overall user experience. Use subtle enhancements such as refined borders, soft shadows, consistent spacing, improved component states, and professional visual polish. The goal is to create a premium, modern, and clean interface without introducing unnecessary complexity or altering existing workflows.

Reporting Requirements: For every review, implementation, verification, bug fix, or document analysis, provide a concise summary using the following format: Issue - a simple one-sentence explanation of the problem. Root Cause a simple explanation of why the issue occurs. Fix - a simple one-sentence explanation of the implemented solution. Impact - a simple explanation of the improvement achieved. Validation Status - PASS or FAIL for functionality, integrations, authentication, authorization, error handling, type safety, performance, accessibility, security, Knowledge Base integration, and production readiness. Include any remaining concerns, recommendations, or follow-up actions if applicable.
